  "id": "glutamate-receptor",
  "term": "glutamate receptor",
  "definition": "A glutamate receptor is a protein on a cell’s surface that binds glutamate and changes how the cell behaves. Some types directly open ion channels, while others work through internal signaling systems; in the central nervous system, these receptors are major drivers of fast excitatory signaling and are linked with memory.",
